From: Neutron <neutron@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Report the host NVIDIA driver's version in Windows' format (NEUTRON_GPU_DRIVER_VERSION).

What he saw: Filmora 16's "Graphics Card Detection Results -- GPU acceleration disabled ... NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 --
Graphics card mismatches with driver": "it recognizes the gpu but claims the driver is mismatched?"

Mechanism: Wine writes one fixed driver version per vendor (NVIDIA "35.0.15.6094" = public driver 560.94, older than
any driver an RTX 50 card runs on Windows) into the display class key's DriverVersion (WMI Win32_VideoController
.DriverVersion, which Filmora's gpu_check reads), DEVPKEY_Device_DriverVersion (SetupAPI), and a different constant
(35.0.15.8180) into the DirectX key. The version never changes when the host driver is updated.
NOT the cause of the box (SOLID, see lab evidence): the box is OpenCL (separate patch, opencl). What this patch does
for Filmora: Filmora keeps its GPU check's result per driver version and re-runs the check only when the version
changes; an install that already turned the GPU off (the box's Close) turns it back on only through a new version.
With the fixed string that never happens; with the host's version it happens on this update and on every host driver
update after it, as a Windows driver update does.

Windows behavior (cited, not measured on his PC): NVIDIA's Windows version ends in the public driver number -- the last
digit of the third field and the fourth field (32.0.15.7628 = 576.28, DXVK dxgi_adapter.cpp; Filmora's own downloaded
blocklist lists real ones as 31.0.15.5161, 31.0.15.2879 and derives "3.6451" = 364.51 from 2x.x.13.6451). The first
field is the WDDM generation (31, 32); upstream Wine b48f03501bf deliberately moved it to 35 ("a future version") and
this patch keeps Wine's 35.0. Probe for his Windows PC: team/fgpu2/probe/drvver.exe (prints SetupAPI, class key, WMI,
DXGI UMD and DirectX key versions plus the registered OpenCL drivers; read-only, exits by itself).

Fix: get_vulkan_gpus() chains VkPhysicalDeviceDriverProperties (when the host device has VK_KHR_driver_properties);
for driverID NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY the Windows string is "35.0.<10 + major/100>.<major%100><minor:02>" from
VkPhysicalDeviceProperties::driverVersion (host 620.70.06 -> 35.0.16.2070). It goes to the class key, the DEVPKEY and
(as a QWORD) the DirectX key. No per-app logic.

Not covered: Mesa (RADV, ANV, NVK) and AMD's own Vulkan driver number releases unrelated to the Windows Adrenalin/Intel
builds, so there is no faithful mapping and they keep Wine's fixed strings. A Linux minor above 99 (535.104) shows as
.99 of the same branch. The Linux and Windows minors of one NVIDIA branch differ (Linux 580.65 vs Windows 580.88); the
branch is exact, the minor is the host's. DXVK's dxgi CheckInterfaceSupport UMD version stays DXVK's own constant
(35.0.19.9999 for NVIDIA). The driver date stays "today" (Wine's).

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-194fv = 194fg + this win32u + the opencl fix; desk fgpu2; team/fgpu2/NOTES.md):
  Probe drvver.exe under Wine: 194fg 35.0.15.6094 (DirectX key 35.0.15.8180); 194fv 35.0.16.2070 in SetupAPI, class
  key, WMI and DirectX key (2/2); NEUTRON_GPU_DRIVER_VERSION=0: 6094/8180 again (1/1).
  Filmora 16 fresh installs (programs install, installer-started copy): Filmora read 35.0.16.2070 (fix, 2/2) vs
  35.0.15.6094 (kill, 2/2); without working OpenCL the box showed in all 4 (result 3), with it in none of 4 (result 0):
  the version does not decide the box.
  Recovery (an install whose box was Closed, GPU off, then a menu launch with working OpenCL): checked version
  6094 -> now 2070: Filmora re-ran its check, result 0, GPU acceleration back on (2/2); same version 2070 -> 2070: no
  re-check, GPU stays off (2/2).
  Kill switch: NEUTRON_GPU_DRIVER_VERSION=0 -> Wine's fixed strings for every vendor.

---
--- a/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
+++ b/dlls/win32u/win32u_private.h
@@ -244,6 +244,9 @@
     char *name;
     GUID uuid;
     ULONGLONG memory;
+    /* NEUTRON: the host driver's version in Windows' display driver format ("35.0.16.2070"), or empty when
+     * there is no faithful mapping (see d3dkmt.c, gpu_driver_version_from_host). */
+    char driver_version[32];
 };
 
 extern BOOL get_vulkan_gpus( struct list *gpus );
--- a/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c
@@ -954,8 +954,48 @@
     VkPhysicalDeviceProperties2 properties2;
     VkPhysicalDeviceIDProperties id;
     VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties mem_properties;
+    VkPhysicalDeviceDriverProperties driver; /* NEUTRON: valid when has_driver is set */
+    BOOL has_driver;
 };
 
+/* NEUTRON: the host driver's version in the format Windows' display driver reports it (the DriverVersion of the
+ * display class key, read by WMI's Win32_VideoController and SetupAPI's DEVPKEY_Device_DriverVersion, and of the
+ * DirectX key). Wine wrote one fixed version per vendor; for NVIDIA that is "35.0.15.6094", i.e. public driver 560.94,
+ * which no RTX 50 card can run on Windows (they need 572 or later) and which never changes when the host driver is
+ * updated. Programs that keep a GPU check's result until the driver changes never saw an update: Filmora 16 re-runs
+ * its check only for a new driver version, so a GPU it had turned off stayed off.
+ *
+ * NVIDIA's Windows version ends in the public driver number: the last digit of the third field and the four
+ * digits of the fourth field are the public major.minor (32.0.15.7628 = 576.28, 32.0.15.6094 = 560.94). The
+ * proprietary Linux driver reports the same public numbering in VkPhysicalDeviceProperties::driverVersion
+ * (major 10 bits, minor 8 bits), so the branch maps exactly; a Linux minor above 99 (535.104) has no Windows
+ * equivalent and is shown as .99 of the same branch. The first two fields stay Wine's ("35.0").
+ * Mesa (RADV, ANV, NVK) and AMD's own Vulkan driver number their releases unrelated to the Windows drivers, so
+ * there is no faithful mapping: those keep Wine's fixed string (empty here).
+ * NEUTRON_GPU_DRIVER_VERSION=0 keeps Wine's fixed strings for every vendor. */
+static void gpu_driver_version_from_host( const struct vk_physdev_info *info, char *buffer, size_t size )
+{
+    static int enabled = -1;
+    UINT32 version, major, minor;
+
+    buffer[0] = 0;
+    if (enabled < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_GPU_DRIVER_VERSION" );
+        enabled = !(e && e[0] == '0');
+    }
+    if (!enabled || !info->has_driver) return;
+    if (info->driver.driverID != VK_DRIVER_ID_NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY) return;
+
+    version = info->properties2.properties.driverVersion;
+    major = version >> 22;
+    minor = (version >> 14) & 0xff;
+    if (major < 100 || major > 999) return;
+    if (minor > 99) minor = 99;
+    snprintf( buffer, size, "35.0.%u.%u%02u", 10 + major / 100, major % 100, minor );
+    TRACE( "host driver %s (%#x) -> %s\n", debugstr_a(info->driver.driverInfo), version, buffer );
+}
+
 static int compare_vulkan_physical_devices( const void *v1, const void *v2 )
 {
     static const int device_type_rank[6] = { 100, 1, 0, 2, 3, 200 };
@@ -985,6 +1025,12 @@
         devinfo[i].id.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_ID_PROPERTIES;
         devinfo[i].properties2.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_PROPERTIES_2;
         devinfo[i].properties2.pNext = &devinfo[i].id;
+        if (physical_device->extensions.has_VK_KHR_driver_properties)
+        {
+            devinfo[i].driver.sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_DRIVER_PROPERTIES;
+            devinfo[i].id.pNext = &devinfo[i].driver;
+            devinfo[i].has_driver = TRUE;
+        }
 
         instance->p_vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2KHR( physical_device->host.physical_device, &devinfo[i].properties2 );
         instance->p_vkGetPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties( physical_device->host.physical_device, &devinfo[i].mem_properties );
@@ -1000,6 +1046,7 @@
         gpu->name = strdup( devinfo[i].properties2.properties.deviceName );
         gpu->pci_id.vendor = devinfo[i].properties2.properties.vendorID;
         gpu->pci_id.device = devinfo[i].properties2.properties.deviceID;
+        gpu_driver_version_from_host( &devinfo[i], gpu->driver_version, sizeof(gpu->driver_version) );
 
         for (j = 0; j < devinfo[i].mem_properties.memoryHeapCount; j++)
         {
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -1469,9 +1469,21 @@
     return default_name;
 };
 
+/* NEUTRON: the DirectX key's DriverVersion (a QWORD, one WORD per field) for the same version string. */
+static UINT64 driver_version_to_qword( const char *version )
+{
+    unsigned int f[4];
+
+    if (sscanf( version, "%u.%u.%u.%u", &f[0], &f[1], &f[2], &f[3] ) != 4) return 0;
+    return ((UINT64)(f[0] & 0xffff) << 48) | ((UINT64)(f[1] & 0xffff) << 32) | ((f[2] & 0xffff) << 16) | (f[3] & 0xffff);
+}
+
 static BOOL write_gpu_to_registry( const struct gpu *gpu, const struct pci_id *pci,
-                                   ULONGLONG memory_size )
+                                   ULONGLONG memory_size, const char *host_driver_version )
 {
+    /* NEUTRON: the host driver's version when it maps onto the vendor's Windows numbering, else Wine's fixed one */
+    const char *driver_version = host_driver_version && host_driver_version[0]
+                                 ? host_driver_version : driver_vendor_to_version( pci->vendor );
     unsigned int size, name_size = (wcslen( gpu->name ) + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR);
     char buffer[4096], *tmp;
     WCHAR bufferW[512];
@@ -1540,7 +1552,7 @@
     if ((subkey = reg_create_ascii_key( hkey, devpkey_device_driver_version, 0, NULL )))
     {
         set_reg_value( subkey, NULL, 0xffff0000 | DEVPROP_TYPE_STRING, bufferW,
-                       asciiz_to_unicode( bufferW, driver_vendor_to_version( pci->vendor ) ));
+                       asciiz_to_unicode( bufferW, driver_version ));
         NtClose( subkey );
     }
 
@@ -1626,7 +1638,7 @@
     value = (ULONG)min( memory_size, (ULONGLONG)MAXDWORD );
     set_reg_value( hkey, memory_sizeW, REG_DWORD, &value, sizeof(value) );
 
-    set_reg_ascii_value( hkey, "DriverVersion", driver_vendor_to_version( pci->vendor ) );
+    set_reg_ascii_value( hkey, "DriverVersion", driver_version );
     NtClose( hkey );
 
 
@@ -1639,6 +1651,10 @@
     {
         UINT64 ver = 0x230000000f1ff4; /* Some version in the future. */
 
+        /* NEUTRON: the same version as the class key when it is the host's */
+        if (driver_version != driver_vendor_to_version( pci->vendor ) && driver_version_to_qword( driver_version ))
+            ver = driver_version_to_qword( driver_version );
+
         asciiz_to_unicode( bufferW, "AdapterLuid" );
         set_reg_value( hkey, bufferW, REG_QWORD, &gpu->luid, sizeof(gpu->luid) );
         asciiz_to_unicode( bufferW, "DriverVersion" );
@@ -1798,7 +1814,7 @@
     if (!memory && opengl_gpu) memory = opengl_gpu->memory;
     if (!memory) memory = 1024 * 1024 * 1024;
 
-    if (!write_gpu_to_registry( gpu, pci_id, memory ))
+    if (!write_gpu_to_registry( gpu, pci_id, memory, vulkan_gpu ? vulkan_gpu->driver_version : NULL ))
     {
         WARN( "Failed to write gpu %p to registry\n", gpu );
         gpu_release( gpu );
